The Toronto Preservation Board recommends that:

1. City Council approve the alterations to the designated heritage property at 420-444 Yonge Street and 1-23 College Street, with conditions, under Part IV, Section 33 of the Ontario Heritage Act, to allow for the construction of the three mixed-use tall buildings, with such alterations to the designated heritage property being substantially in accordance with plans and drawings dated January 23, 2026, prepared by Hariri Pontarini Architects and on file with the Senior Manager, Heritage Planning, and the Heritage Impact Assessment prepared by ERA Architects Inc., dated July 4, 2025 as revised on April 17, 2026, and on file with the Senior Manager, Heritage Planning, all subject to and in accordance with the Conservation Plan satisfactory to the Senior Manager, Heritage Planning.

